  "slug": "forecasting-infectious-0468",
  "summary": "A German multi-model respiratory forecasting ensemble appears alongside preprints on epidemic heterogeneity and cytokine feedback in avian coronavirus infection.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is model-based quantification of infection dynamics, with each item pairing an explicit model class with data. The only published item is a real-time multi-model, multi-target ensemble for German ARI, SARI, influenza and RSV activity in the 2024/25 season. One preprint adapts turbulence decomposition to epidemiological data and introduces the Epimetheus network simulator, using scale-dependent fluctuations to probe population heterogeneity in the 2020/21 period. The other models avian coronavirus host-virus interactions, identifying cytokine feedback as a driver of strain-specific immune response. Relative to case-count forecasting alone, the new emphasis is on unobserved structure: population heterogeneity and feedback between viral dynamics and innate immunity. The items address different scales and are not directly comparable.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
